\mt1 Colossians
\c 1
\s1 Greetings from Paul and Timothy
\r (\ref Philippians 1:1–2|PHP 1:1-2\ref*; \ref Philemon 1:1–3|PHM 1-3\ref*)
\p \v 1 Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by \add the\add* will of God, and Timothy \add our\add* brother,
\p \v 2 To the saints and faithful brothers in Christ at Colossae:
\p Grace and peace to you from God our Father.\f + \fr 1:2 \ft BYZ and TR \fqa God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ\f*
\s1 Thanksgiving and Prayer
\r (\ref 1 Corinthians 1:4–9|1CO 1:4-9\ref*; \ref Philippians 1:3–11|PHP 1:3-11\ref*)
\p \v 3 We always thank God, \add the\add* Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, when we pray for you, \v 4 because we have heard about your faith in Christ Jesus and your love for all the saints — \v 5 \add the faith and love\add* proceeding from the hope stored up for you in heaven, of which you have already heard in the word of truth, the gospel \v 6 that has come to you.
\p All over the world \add this gospel\add* is bearing fruit and growing, just as \add it has been doing\add* among you since the day you heard \add it\add* and truly understood the grace of God. \v 7 You learned \add it\add* from Epaphras, our beloved fellow servant, who is a faithful minister of Christ on our\f + \fr 1:7 \ft NE, NA, BYZ, and TR \fqa your\f* behalf, \v 8 \add and\add* who also informed us of your love in \add the\add* Spirit.
\p \v 9 For this reason, since the day we heard \add about you\add*, we \add have\add* not stopped praying for you and asking \add God\add* to fill you with the knowledge of His will in all spiritual wisdom and understanding, \v 10 so that you may walk in a manner worthy of the Lord \add and\add* may please \add Him\add* in every way: bearing fruit in every good work, growing in the knowledge of God, \v 11 being strengthened with all power according to His glorious might so that you may have full endurance and patience, \add and\add* joyfully \v 12 giving thanks to the Father, who has qualified you\f + \fr 1:12 \ft BYZ and TR \fqa us\f* to share in the inheritance of the saints in the light.
\p \v 13 He has rescued us from the dominion of darkness and brought \add us\add* into the kingdom of His beloved Son, \v 14 in whom we have redemption,\f + \fr 1:14 \ft TR \fqa redemption through His blood,\f* the forgiveness of sins.
\s1 The Supremacy of the Son
\r (\ref Hebrews 1:1–14|HEB 1:1-14\ref*)
\p \v 15 \add The Son\add* is \add the\add* image of the invisible God, \add the\add* firstborn over all creation. \v 16 For in Him all things were created, \add things\add* in heaven and on earth, visible and invisible, whether thrones or dominions or rulers or authorities. All things were created through Him and for Him.
\p \v 17 He is before all things, and in Him all things hold together. \v 18 And He is the head of the body, the church; He is the beginning \add and\add* firstborn from among the dead, so that in all things He may have preeminence. \v 19 For \add God\add* was pleased \add to have\add* all \add His\add* fullness dwell in Him, \v 20 and through Him to reconcile to Himself all things, whether things on earth or things in heaven, by making peace through the blood of His cross.
\p \v 21 Once you were alienated  \add from God \add* and were hostile in your minds, engaging in evil deeds. \v 22 But now He has reconciled \add you\add* by \add Christ’s\add* physical body through death to present you holy, unblemished, and blameless in His presence — \v 23 if indeed you continue in \add your\add* faith, established and firm, not moved from the hope of the gospel you heard, which has been proclaimed to every creature\f + \fr 1:23 \ft Or \fqa in all creation\f* under heaven, \add and\add* of which I, Paul, have become a servant.
\s1 Paul’s Suffering for the Church
\r (\ref 2 Corinthians 11:16–33|2CO 11:16-33\ref*)
\p \v 24 Now I rejoice in \add my\add* sufferings for you, and I fill up in my flesh what is lacking in regard to Christ’s afflictions for the sake of His body, which is the church. \v 25 I became its servant by the commission God gave me to fully proclaim to you the word of God, \v 26 the mystery that was hidden for ages and generations but is now revealed to His saints. \v 27 To \add them\add* God has chosen to make known among the Gentiles the glorious riches of this mystery, which is Christ in you, the hope of glory.
\p \v 28 We proclaim Him, admonishing and teaching everyone with all wisdom, so that we may present everyone perfect\f + \fr 1:28 \ft Or \fqa fully mature\f* in Christ. \v 29 To this end I also labor, striving with all His energy working powerfully within me.
\c 2
\s1 Absent in Body, Present in Spirit
\r (\ref Revelation 3:14–22|REV 3:14-22\ref*)
\p \v 1 For I want you to know how much I am struggling for you and \add for\add* those at Laodicea, and for all who have not met me face to face, \v 2 that they may be encouraged in heart, knit together in love, and filled with \add the\add* full riches of complete understanding, so that they may know the mystery of God, \add namely\add* Christ,\f + \fr 2:2 \ft Literally \fqa the mystery of God: Christ\f* \v 3 in whom are hidden all the treasures of wisdom and knowledge.
\p \v 4 I say this so that no one will deceive you by smooth rhetoric. \v 5 For although I am absent from you in body, I am present with you in spirit, \add and\add* I delight to see your orderly condition and firm faith in Christ.
\s1 Alive with Christ
\r (\ref Ephesians 2:1–10|EPH 2:1-10\ref*)
\p \v 6 Therefore, just as you have received Christ Jesus \add as\add* Lord, continue to walk in Him, \v 7 rooted and built up in Him, established in the faith as you were taught, \add and\add* overflowing with thankfulness.
\p \v 8 See to it that no one takes you captive through philosophy and empty deception, which are based on human tradition \add and\add* the spiritual forces of the world rather than on Christ. \v 9 For in \add Christ\add* all the fullness of the Deity dwells in bodily form. \v 10 And you have been made complete in \add Christ\add*, who is the head over every ruler and authority.
\p \v 11 In Him you were also circumcised, in the putting off of \add your\add* sinful nature, with the circumcision \add performed\add* by Christ\f + \fr 2:11 \ft Literally \fqa in the cutting away of the body of the flesh, by the circumcision of Christ\f* \add and\add* not by human hands. \v 12 And having been buried with Him in baptism, you were raised with \add Him\add* through \add your\add* faith in the power of God, who raised Him from the dead.
\p \v 13 \add When\add* you were dead in \add your\add* trespasses and in the uncircumcision of your sinful nature, God made you alive with \add Christ\add*. He forgave us all \add our\add* trespasses, \v 14 having canceled the debt ascribed to us in the decrees that stood against us. He took it away, nailing it to the cross! \v 15 \add And\add* having disarmed the powers and authorities, He made a public spectacle \add of them\add*, triumphing over them by \add the cross\add*.
\p \v 16 Therefore \add let\add* no one judge you by what you eat or drink, or with regard to a feast, a New Moon, or a Sabbath. \v 17 These are a shadow of the things to come, but the body  \add that casts it \add* belongs to Christ.\f + \fr 2:17 \ft Literally \fqa but the body is of the Christ\f* \v 18 \add Do not let anyone\add* who delights in \add false\add* humility and \add the\add* worship of angels disqualify you with speculation about what he has seen. \add Such a person\add* is puffed up without basis by his unspiritual mind. \v 19 He has lost connection to the head, from whom the whole body, supported and knit together by \add its\add* joints and ligaments, grows as God causes it to grow.
\p \v 20 If you have died with Christ to the spiritual forces of the world, why, as though you still belonged to \add the\add* world, do you submit to \add its\add* regulations: \v 21 “\add Do\add* not handle, \add do\add* not taste, \add do\add* not touch!”? \v 22 \add These\add* will all perish with use, because they are based on human commands and teachings. \v 23 Such \add restrictions\add* indeed have an appearance of wisdom, with \add their\add* self-prescribed worship, \add their false\add* humility, and \add their\add* harsh treatment of \add the\add* body; \add but\add* they are of no value against \add the\add* indulgence of the flesh.
\c 3
\s1 Put On the New Self
\r (\ref Ephesians 4:17–32|EPH 4:17-32\ref*)
\p \v 1 Therefore, since you have been raised with Christ, strive for the things above, where Christ is seated at \add the\add* right hand of God. \v 2 Set \add your\add* minds on things above, not on earthly things. \v 3 For you died, and your life is now hidden with Christ in God. \v 4 When Christ, who is your\f + \fr 3:4 \ft NE, WH, BYZ, and TR \fqa our\f* life, appears, then you also will appear with Him in glory.
\p \v 5 Put to death, therefore, the components of your earthly nature: sexual immorality, impurity, lust, evil desires, and greed, which is idolatry. \v 6 Because of these, the wrath of God is coming on the sons of disobedience.\f + \fr 3:6 \ft NE, WH, and Tischendorf do not include \fqa on the sons of disobedience\ft .\f* \v 7 When you lived among them, you also used to walk in these ways. \v 8 But now you must put aside all such things as these: anger, rage, malice, slander, \add and\add* filthy language from your lips.
\p \v 9 \add Do\add* not lie to one another, since you have taken off the old self with \add its\add* practices, \v 10 and have put on the new \add self\add*, which is being renewed in knowledge in \add the\add* image of \add its\add* Creator. \v 11 Here there is no Greek \add or\add* Jew, circumcised \add or\add* uncircumcised, barbarian, Scythian, slave, \add or\add* free, but Christ \add is\add* all and \add is\add* in all.
\p \v 12 Therefore, as \add the\add* elect of God, holy and beloved, clothe yourselves with hearts of compassion, kindness, humility, gentleness, \add and\add* patience. \v 13 Bear with one another and forgive \add any\add* complaint you may have against someone else. Forgive as the Lord forgave you. \v 14 And over all these \add virtues put on\add* love, which is \add the\add* bond of perfect unity. \v 15 \add Let\add* the peace of Christ rule in your hearts, \add for\add* to this you were called as members of one body. And be thankful.
\p \v 16 \add Let\add* the word of Christ richly dwell within you as you teach and admonish one another with all wisdom, \add and\add* as you sing psalms, hymns, \add and\add* spiritual songs with gratitude in your hearts to God. \v 17 And whatever you do, in word or deed, \add do it\add* all in \add the\add* name of \add the\add* Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God \add the\add* Father through Him.
\s1 Christian Households
\r (\ref Ephesians 6:1–4|EPH 6:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 18 Wives, submit to \add your\add* husbands, as is fitting in \add the\add* Lord.
\p \v 19 Husbands, love \add your\add* wives and \add do\add* not be harsh with them.
\p \v 20 Children, obey \add your\add* parents in everything, for this is pleasing to \add the\add* Lord.
\p \v 21 Fathers, \add do\add* not provoke your children, so they will not become discouraged.
\s1 Serving with Honor
\r (\ref Ephesians 6:5–9|EPH 6:5-9\ref*; \ref 1 Timothy 6:1–2|1TI 6:1-2\ref*)
\p \v 22 Slaves, obey \add your\add* earthly masters in everything, not \add only\add* to please them while they are watching, but with sincerity of heart \add and\add* fear of the Lord.
\p \v 23 Whatever you do, work at it with your whole being, as for the Lord and not for men, \v 24 because you know that you will receive an inheritance from \add the\add* Lord \add as your\add* reward. \add It is\add* the Lord Christ you are serving. \v 25 Whoever does wrong will be repaid \add for\add* his wrong, and there is no favoritism.
\c 4
\s1 Prayerful Speech and Actions
\p \v 1 Masters, supply \add your\add* slaves with what \add is\add* right and fair, since you know that you also have a Master in heaven.
\p \v 2 Devote yourselves to prayer, being watchful \add and\add* thankful, \v 3 as you pray also for us, that God may open to us a door for the word, so that we may proclaim the mystery of Christ, for which I am in chains. \v 4 \add Pray\add* that I may declare it clearly, as I should.
\p \v 5 Act wisely toward outsiders, redeeming the time. \v 6 \add Let\add* your speech always \add be\add* gracious, seasoned with salt, so that you may know how to answer everyone.
\s1 Greetings from Paul’s Fellow Workers
\r (\ref Romans 16:21–23|ROM 16:21-23\ref*)
\p \v 7 Tychicus will tell you all the news about me. \add He is\add* a beloved brother, a faithful minister, and a fellow servant in \add the\add* Lord. \v 8 I have sent him to you for this very purpose, that you may know about us, and that he may encourage your hearts. \v 9 With him \add I am sending\add* Onesimus, \add our\add* faithful and beloved brother, who is \add one\add* of you. They will tell you \add about\add* everything here.
\p \v 10 My fellow prisoner Aristarchus sends you greetings, as does Mark the cousin of Barnabas. You have \add already\add* received instructions about \add him\add*: If he comes to you, welcome him. \v 11 Jesus, who is called Justus, also \add sends greetings\add*. These are \add the\add* only Jews among \add my\add* fellow workers for the kingdom of God, \add and\add* they have been a comfort to me.
\p \v 12 Epaphras, who \add is one\add* of you \add and\add* a servant of Christ Jesus, sends you greetings. \add He is\add* always wrestling in prayer for you, so that you may stand mature and fully assured in \add the\add* full will of God. \v 13 For I testify about him that he goes to great pains for you and for those at Laodicea and Hierapolis.
\p \v 14 Luke, the beloved physician, and Demas send you greetings.
\s1 Signature and Final Instructions
\r (\ref 1 Corinthians 16:19–24|1CO 16:19-24\ref*; \ref 2 Thessalonians 3:16–18|2TH 3:16-18\ref*)
\p \v 15 Greet the brothers in Laodicea, as well as Nympha and the church \add that meets\add* at her house.
\p \v 16 After \add this\add* letter has been read among you, make sure that it is also read in the church of \add the\add* Laodiceans, and that you in turn read the \add letter\add* from Laodicea.
\p \v 17 Tell Archippus: “See to it that you complete the ministry you have received in \add the\add* Lord.”
\p \v 18 This greeting \add is in my\add* own hand — Paul.
\p Remember my chains.
\p Grace \add be\add* with you.\f + \fr 4:18 \ft BYZ and TR include \fqa Amen.\f*
